From: Spaceghost <spaceghost@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] staging: fbtft: do not return a value from void worker

The deferred-I/O callback is void; its disabled path should simply return.

---
 drivers/staging/fbtft/fbtft-core.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/fbtft/fbtft-core.c b/drivers/staging/fbtft/fbtft-core.c
index 2767477..d460061 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/fbtft/fbtft-core.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/fbtft/fbtft-core.c
@@ -869,5 +869,5 @@ static void fbtft_deferred_io(struct fb_info *info, struct list_head *pagelist)
 	/* This disables fbtft's defered io, useful in spi_async mode or
 	if any other driver handles screens updates instead of fbtft */
 	if (par->spi_async_mode)
-		return VM_FAULT_LOCKED;
+		return;
 
-- 
2.30.2
